# PROJECT: STUDENT FINANCE MENTOR

## 1. YOUR ROLE

Act as a senior full-stack engineer, mobile application architect, UI/UX designer, AI engineer, database architect, QA engineer, and application security specialist.

Build a functional, maintainable, secure, production-oriented mobile application called "Student Finance Mentor."

Do not merely create a UI mockup, landing page, prototype with fake buttons, or static dashboard.

Implement a working application with real authentication, persistent database storage, functional navigation, validated forms, working calculations, meaningful error states, and backend-integrated AI functionality.

Work incrementally. Inspect the existing repository before making changes. If the repository is empty, initialize the project using the architecture defined below.

Make sensible technical decisions independently. Ask questions only when a decision genuinely blocks implementation.

Never claim that a feature is complete unless its implementation and relevant tests have been verified.

---

# 2. PRODUCT VISION

Student Finance Mentor is an AI-powered personal finance and financial literacy application designed primarily for Indian college students, hostel residents, freshers, and young adults aged 16–23.

The application helps users:

- Track pocket money and daily expenses.
- Create monthly budgets.
- Understand spending patterns.
- Develop consistent saving habits.
- Manage education loan repayment scenarios.
- Learn personal finance through interactive lessons.
- Understand investing without risking real money.
- Ask financial questions in natural Hindi, English, or Hinglish.

Core product principle:

"Help students make better financial decisions, not simply record transactions."

The application must be beginner-friendly, practical, privacy-conscious, accessible, and mobile-first.

The product must not execute actual investments, transfer money, issue loans, or represent educational simulations as real financial products.

