# 3. TARGET USERS AND USE CASES

Primary users:
- Indian college students.
- Students living in hostels or PG accommodation.
- Students receiving monthly pocket money.
- Fresh graduates starting their first jobs.
- Young adults learning personal finance.

Example user scenarios:

1. A student receives ₹4,000 every month and wants to save ₹800.
2. A hostel resident wants to understand why food expenses are increasing.
3. A student wants an alert when 80% of the food budget has been used.
4. A borrower wants to estimate education loan EMI and total interest.
5. A beginner wants to learn SIPs and compound interest.
6. A student wants to practise investing using virtual money.
7. A user asks the AI coach a question in Hinglish.

All examples must use Indian rupees and the Asia/Kolkata timezone by default.

Support localization-ready architecture. English can be the initial interface language, while the AI coach must understand Hindi, English, and Hinglish.

